        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear Colleague, I am writing to inform you regarding our mutual patient, an 81-year-old female admitted on 23/04/2004 with an acute exacerbation of her known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, she presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Clinical examination confirmed bilateral expiratory wheeze. Chest X-ray showed hyperinflation without consolidation. Arterial blood gas analysis revealed mild hypoxaemia. Blood tests showed mildly elevated inflammatory markers. She was treated with nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, and supplemental oxygen, with good clinical response. Vital signs were monitored closely throughout her stay. She was discharged home in a stable condition. I recommend continued optimisation of her inhaled therapy and close follow-up in your practice. Please do not hesitate to contact me should you require further information.</div>"
            },
